# Component Conventions

## Routing

Use React Router for all navigation. Never use `useState` to switch between screens.

```tsx
import { useNavigate, useParams } from "react-router";

export default function VotePage() {
  const { id } = useParams<{ id: string }>();
  const navigate = useNavigate();

  const handleComplete = () => navigate(`/trip/${id}/results`);
  const handleBack = () => navigate(-1);
}
```

## Page Animations (Framer Motion)

Wrap every page in a `motion.div` with horizontal slide transitions. Use `AnimatePresence` in `App.tsx` around the `<Routes>` outlet.

```tsx
import { motion } from "motion/react";

const pageVariants = {
  enter: { x: "100%", opacity: 0 },
  center: { x: 0, opacity: 1, transition: { duration: 0.3, ease: [0.22, 1, 0.36, 1] } },
  exit: { x: "-50%", opacity: 0, transition: { duration: 0.2 } },
};

export default function SomePage() {
  return (
    <motion.div variants={pageVariants} initial="enter" animate="center" exit="exit">
      {/* page content */}
    </motion.div>
  );
}
```

Card transitions use scale + fade:

```tsx
const cardVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 20, scale: 0.97 },
  visible: { opacity: 1, y: 0, scale: 1, transition: { duration: 0.38, ease: [0.22, 1, 0.36, 1] } },
  exit: { opacity: 0, y: -10, scale: 0.97, transition: { duration: 0.28 } },
};
```

## State Access

Read shared data from the Zustand store. Use `useState` only for component-local UI state (modal open, animation phase, pressed state).

```tsx
import { useTripStore } from "@/lib/store";

export default function SomePage() {
  const activities = useTripStore((s) => s.currentTrip.activities);
  const vote = useTripStore((s) => s.recordVote);
}
```

## File Organization

- Pages (routed) → `/src/pages/`
- Reusable UI components → `/src/components/`
- Sub-components (like `ActivityCardInner`) stay in the same file as their parent
- Shared shadcn/radix primitives stay in `/src/app/components/ui/` — prefer using these for sheets, dialogs, and form inputs over building custom ones

## Touch Targets

Every interactive element must be at least 44px tall. Use `min-h-11` (44px) on buttons, links, and tappable cards. This is a mobile app — fat-finger-proof everything.

## Bottom Sheets

Use the existing `vaul` Drawer component (already installed, shadcn `Drawer` in `ui/drawer.tsx`) for bottom sheets like SalvageModal and CreateTripSheet. Configure with drag-to-dismiss.
